<node id="Comparative Analysis of Layer Types in Sequence Models (table)">
  <data key="d0">Comparative Analysis of Layer Types in Sequence Models (table)</data>
  <data key="d1">table</data>
  <data key="d2">This table compares the computational complexity, sequential operations, and maximum path lengths of self-attention, recurrent, and convolutional layers. It illustrates the efficiency of self-attention in handling long-range dependencies, supporting the surrounding content's focus on the advantages of self-attention in sequence transduction tasks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e28d338d86871fa791c09446f219838</data>
  <data key="d4">attention.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1763841259</data>
</node>
<node id="Positional Encoding Formula (equation)">
  <data key="d0">Positional Encoding Formula (equation)</data>
  <data key="d1">equation</data>
  <data key="d2">This equation defines the positional encodings used in the Transformer model, allowing the model to incorporate the order of tokens in sequences, which is essential for tasks like translation and text processing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0a04ac1a806619e1fb130a04019990e</data>
  <data key="d4">attention.pdf</data>
